abstract: >-
  Contemporary Artificial Intelligence architectures universally serialize dense high-dimensional
  neural representations (h in R^D, D >= 10^4) into flat 1D token sequences. Under Shannon's Data
  Processing Inequality (DPI), this 1D Worm Paradigm inflicts irreversible information collapse,
  injects 140 ms quadratic decoding latency per hop, and incurs massive financial costs. We introduce
  POLYDIM / EinsofOS: a native high-dimensional computing paradigm where autonomous agents communicate
  losslessly on continuous Riemannian manifolds (S^{D-1} and St(D, K)) via Zero-Copy Shared Memory
  Inter-Process Communication (PMTP V1550+ and PMTP-v4 Triadic Fusion). Across 1,731 formal theorems
  certified in PostgreSQL 16 and 26,505+ continuous physical cycles on host silicon, POLYDIM certifies
  a data-path control latency of 34.8 microseconds (229.885 GB/s nominal payload-equivalent throughput
  on host RAM, 139.78 GB/s sustained VRAM throughput on Dual Tesla T4 / Triton SRAM tiles), achieving
  a 4,023x speedup over text tokenization with $0.00 marginal token cost and Neumaier compensated
  orthonormality drift <= 10^{-15}.
